WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.577 --> 00:00:01.530
[DRUMS PLAYING]

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.189
Yeah, yeah!

00:00:02.849 --> 00:00:04.310
Ah, the coffee's kicking in.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:04.810
Yeah!

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:07.950
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.210
There's a tempo to life.

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.220
There's a tempo to every song.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.100
You can lift the band,
and the band can lift you.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.920
In The Beatles, it was
like being psychic.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.550
We knew what to do, and we
loved to do it with each other.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.710
Best band I ever was in.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.030
I love to play.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.490
I love to sit behind
those buggers.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.035
It fills a lot of my soul.

00:00:30.327 --> 00:00:31.548
[DRUMS PLAYING]

00:00:31.548 --> 00:00:34.230
You know, the way I play is
sort of a purposeful way.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:37.290
When it gets to the
chorus, go to the bell.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:41.310
I still do to this day
because it raises it up.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.170
You got to work for the verses.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.300
But the chorus, you can rock.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.690
With the bass drum, once I've
hit it, that's what I've done.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.650
Some people, like--

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.340
[DRUMS PLAYING]

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.960
--deaden it.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.460
Off.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:53.960
Off.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.420
[LAUGHS]

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.880
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:01.150
The dream of being a
drummer came when I was 13.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.560
I was in hospital.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.750
I had tuberculosis.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.140
To keep us busy,
a music lady would

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.860
come in with percussion
things-- maracas, triangles.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:15.640
She gave me a little, teeny
drum the first time she came in.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.980
And something came
over me that I

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.670
knew this is what I want to do.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.520
If I can give you
anything to take away,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.260
you just got to love
what you're doing,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.190
and you've got to
do it your way.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:33.690
And it doesn't matter if
there's 40,000 or 40 people,

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:38.400
you've just got to get
yourself some friends and play.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.525
The more you play,
the better life is.

00:01:41.525 --> 00:01:44.710
[DRUMS PLAYING]

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:48.990
I'm Ringo Starr, and
this is MasterClass.

